# Data

Mistake without this: smuggle compose/workflow into catalog JSON, put service semantics on product rows, or swap `execution.json` with `graph.edges.wire`.

**Hub:** `docs/identity.md` · `docs/id.md` · Bugbot: [BUGBOT.md](../../BUGBOT.md)

porto-data is a **factual bundle** + schemas + validators — not UI, compose, or a resolver. One fact per layer.

```text
Lookup dimensions   →  country, weight, envelope?, services (kind), optional product_id / service_ids
Catalog facts       →  id, zones, weights, prices, geometry (this repo)
Layout output       →  mark_profile, size, mark size + placement
Adapter wiring      →  graph.edges.wire productCode
Execution gate      →  execution.json wire + billing/execution tokens
Runtime             →  mark bytes, tracking (not here)
```

1. One identifier, one job — products have concrete `id` only; no `kind` or size-bucket taxonomy.
2. Facts vs normalization vs workflow — workflow stays outside this package.
3. Catalog `id` in graph/prices/rules; `kind` on services/features for cross-operator intent only.
4. `execution.json` ≠ wire tables; `graph.edges.wire` holds checkout codes.
5. Layouts: shared/jurisdiction-standard **window** facts + `standard` only; mark **size** / **placement** on `marks.json`; address forms in `formats/addresses.json` (place field **`locality`**).
6. Validators enforce philosophy — not prose alone.

**Red flags:** compose fields on products; `kind` keys in graph/prices; `productCode` in execution.json; `lane` on products; `city` on address forms; implementor method names in catalog docs.

Before merge: name owning layer → `make validate` → refresh metadata → `make test-cov` → CHANGELOG when catalog-facing.
